# default.aur — AUR packages installed on EVERY machine, whatever its class.
#
# The AUR counterpart to the top-level *.pkgs lists. Layering is identical:
#
#   default.aur        every machine          (this file)
#   class/<role>.aur   the ROLE    — desktop | laptop | work
#   host/<name>.aur    the MACHINE — keyed on the short hostname
#
# gaming.aur sits outside that stack: it is gated on the gaming opt-in, not on
# class, so bootstrap skips it in the glob and adds it only when gaming is on.
#
# Everything here goes through paru, which BUILDS from source. Prefer a repo
# package in a *.pkgs list whenever one exists; a package belongs here only if
# the AUR is the only place it lives.

stably-orca-bin
